on/id #uuid "7f06ce1a-3e13-5308-9a14-0ac2fdb59c56" :question/math-academy-id "q-120655" :question/problem "$\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1}=\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the following identity: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\n$$\n\nUsing the above identity, we can further simplify our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta .\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-120655/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eda44360-52ec-59f7-98b4-f8d866a465e9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120655"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-23853/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "1836c3e5-8364-549e-9400-dcc12cfe17bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-23853/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "608ffb16-f713-5b8c-9a14-64b55486cfe1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-23853/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "502e8efa-9499-5b4d-8535-b5555f676f9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-23853/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "a86b481d-c878-577e-ab56-361bec208dd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-23853/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "dbf669aa-aaa8-5dc3-9ed1-7b4bf8fb23e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-23853/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6c5b65c5-879b-54d2-9ec3-be2a8df72f1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-23853/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-23853/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-23853/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-23853/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-23853/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-23853/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-23853" :question/id #uuid "67303de5-29d5-5458-8cb0-e20946888cb8" :question/math-academy-id "q-23853" :question/problem "Simplify ${sec}^{4}⁡x-2{sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{4}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we can simplify our expression by factoring it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sec}^{4}⁡x-2{sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{4}⁡x & =({sec}^{2}⁡x)^{2}-2{sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x+({tan}^{2}⁡x)^{2} \\\\  & ={({sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can rewrite our expression using $(3),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x)}^{2} & ={(1)}^{2} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{sec}^{4}⁡x-2{sec}^{2}⁡x\\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{4}⁡x=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-23853/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "141d61c7-1d82-52fe-b977-19daa910da9b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-23853"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-120661/selection/5ca5bee31a11dd6944fc79b08ebcd42e90e276b08549e54566a88008161df5f4" :answer/id #uuid "197e5d2b-0490-5d1e-9df6-fe2ed00b2317" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120661/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "cdb6ed41-ea55-5677-bdf6-5a12562d5af4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120661/selection/6efafc0180c7ae7c44bfc5a7db671ae6018a41d2c93941d05a1aff1565575420" :answer/id #uuid "5727e43e-f671-5d86-b524-8654d84c8155" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120661/selection/ff8f1ffdc2cbfb1a4a64c41b9ac9f0be14fabc5b524807351f2d1cd1f9f0e487" :answer/id #uuid "b348568c-3151-59f2-b11c-51c1e0c89d97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120661/selection/9461c1bcc96cbf5bf001cc7da81fa01409a70d358b4d360bd06099fd591a56ef" :answer/id #uuid "f7544206-a06f-5bda-91c9-419443e0139f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120661/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc64d67f-d02d-5bca-b92c-916a37642079" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-120661/selection/5ca5bee31a11dd6944fc79b08ebcd42e90e276b08549e54566a88008161df5f4" :answer-field/choices ["q-120661/selection/5ca5bee31a11dd6944fc79b08ebcd42e90e276b08549e54566a88008161df5f4" "q-120661/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-120661/selection/6efafc0180c7ae7c44bfc5a7db671ae6018a41d2c93941d05a1aff1565575420" "q-120661/selection/ff8f1ffdc2cbfb1a4a64c41b9ac9f0be14fabc5b524807351f2d1cd1f9f0e487" "q-120661/selection/9461c1bcc96cbf5bf001cc7da81fa01409a70d358b4d360bd06099fd591a56ef"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-120661" :question/id #uuid "a4124205-8bba-50c1-a590-cbcdb14b2bc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-120661" :question/problem "Simplify $\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}=\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{{sec}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}\n$$\n\nNext, we can further simplify our expression by factoring it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)^{2}} & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1)}{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1)}{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-120661/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "141d61c7-1d82-52fe-b977-19daa910da9b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120661"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-43292/selection/1af7e13befc2d99c990cb25ccaed11b73211adacccdeb3d96a12ee4830dd54b2" :answer/id #uuid "48d825fe-bae5-5439-86d0-4b62293907aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43292/selection/345b8a3583df13685c259fa391e522412345c1553f022dbc3c1e0c3edf0d1846" :answer/id #uuid "858395bd-093a-58cf-8275-46cbf6e00545" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{tan}^{4}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43292/selection/a0332b537f4486805ad1793740b0a1ac4165eaeb48e40facdc78c5de1981c15a" :answer/id #uuid "c0b4c8d3-ea49-5f91-9764-b50259112ddc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43292/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "83491247-e8cf-5e