{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }}\\frac{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & ={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ({sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ({sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1) & ={tan}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={tan}^{4}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta {tan}^{4}⁡\\theta -{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ={tan}^{4}⁡\\theta .\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-43292/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "141d61c7-1d82-52fe-b977-19daa910da9b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-43292"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-120660/selection/9461c1bcc96cbf5bf001cc7da81fa01409a70d358b4d360bd06099fd591a56ef" :answer/id #uuid "a960312e-d793-5da9-a49d-a65deb66f22d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120660/selection/ea1e338de2a0cb8a640a44950398210d1ca222223a655996523a7e9a1815ad8e" :answer/id #uuid "de81087b-986c-5246-bfbc-3a5c6694b741" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120660/selection/3d22298652b5c90370183e52a0da8a8d7b60c3f177c1f0920e7fc854ceaec73b" :answer/id #uuid "620c5466-603d-566a-955a-98e168b705da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120660/selection/becd4533710b9f087ded8e2997317ac1f8a6869e9b84ab585f0bc3e06bb4b9e2" :answer/id #uuid "b1f0429e-e2a0-5beb-9fa9-deb2343a3d0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120660/selection/46378ad3adc1444aacd916d17d96d0af3fa1a6f83ea50f20802a801e3ebd0bd0" :answer/id #uuid "007808dc-08a1-5b55-a3c3-c37fcb6e4989" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{sec}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120660/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "01714cfe-c53b-536e-93ff-e281bf202852" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-120660/selection/becd4533710b9f087ded8e2997317ac1f8a6869e9b84ab585f0bc3e06bb4b9e2" :answer-field/choices ["q-120660/selection/9461c1bcc96cbf5bf001cc7da81fa01409a70d358b4d360bd06099fd591a56ef" "q-120660/selection/ea1e338de2a0cb8a640a44950398210d1ca222223a655996523a7e9a1815ad8e" "q-120660/selection/3d22298652b5c90370183e52a0da8a8d7b60c3f177c1f0920e7fc854ceaec73b" "q-120660/selection/becd4533710b9f087ded8e2997317ac1f8a6869e9b84ab585f0bc3e06bb4b9e2" "q-120660/selection/46378ad3adc1444aacd916d17d96d0af3fa1a6f83ea50f20802a801e3ebd0bd0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-120660" :question/id #uuid "3a5bb470-9e62-50a9-851a-d9d6f1fb0a5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-120660" :question/problem "Simplify $\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}-1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}-1=\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}-1\n$$\n\nFinally, we can further simplify our expression by factoring the numerator as a difference of squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}-1 & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1)}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1)}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}}-1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-1-1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+1}-1=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-120660/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "141d61c7-1d82-52fe-b977-19daa910da9b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120660"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-65392"] :question/problem "Simplify $\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(3),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}=\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the numerator as a difference of squares, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x} & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-74167/selection/68e7f97ce1d7f1cfa32cdb556f370b2c5ca6ac9601db47f9a9d7e883c47ea597" :answer/id #uuid "4a3dee10-5f8c-544b-9e6a-53608c51bcc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+{tan}^{4}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74167/selection/152718011c35293a1b3ec50edcd628f6d33996fa46affee7e5b09aaca1f3a6cc" :answer/id #uuid "7b8bb6df-9d0a-5566-b621-60c49d2b8ca0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡x+{tan}^{4}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74167/selection/d2058c598527de7c11bc996ce15b7e8d70a0510720f8a997ffa0afb27ee61aa4" :answer/id #uuid "862023a2-8a4b-56e8-a6df-4cfbcec868d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{tan}^{4}⁡x-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74167/selection/e1710ac59b9b2cc22bf45b2465e96860e03fdf977b8c025c4059d48c30755b48" :answer/id #uuid "34e45809-77ac-55fe-a9de-2b7b36595853" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74167/selection/eb402cc63d07a3ed3ad0f034706699dabe9b894820ca0bb49e3b8d794325503c" :answer/id #uuid "0439e24f-a093-5095-996e-597a02208d68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-{tan}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74167/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "16787a52-f969-5089-817e-b7e93ce3f1b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74167/selection/d2058c598527de7c11bc996ce15b7e8d70a0510720f8a997ffa0afb27ee61aa4" :answer-field/choices ["q-74167/selection/68e7f97ce1d7f1cfa32cdb556f370b2c5ca6ac9601db47f9a9d7e883c47ea597" "q-74167/selection/152718011c35293a1b3ec50edcd628f6d33996fa46affee7e5b09aaca1f3a6cc" "q-74167/selection/d2058c598527de7c11bc996ce15b7e8d70a0510720f8a997ffa0afb27ee61aa4" "q-74167/selection/e1710ac59b9b2cc22bf45b2465e96860e03fdf977b8c025c4059d48c30755b48" "q-74167/selection/eb402cc63d07a3ed3ad0f034706699dabe9b894820ca0bb49e3b8d794325503c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74167" :question/id #uuid "3c231bcb-00f5-5c10-87ba-efe156f326e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-74167" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${tan}^{2}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x-1?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & (1) & 1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & (2) & {tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x-1 \\\\  & (3) & {sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify our expression using $(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x-1 & ={tan}^{2}⁡x({sec}^{2}⁡x-1)-1 \\\\  & ={tan}^{2}⁡x({tan}^{2}⁡x)-1 \\\\  & ={tan}^{4}⁡x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x-{tan}^{2}⁡x-1={tan}^{4}⁡x-1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-74167/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b14ef98-8122-512a-9cce-6e44392959d8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74167"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-120807/selection/54661d432eed36afb6f5a8d712e4546a08ef08094e547d421ed7e6f15b72dad8" :answer/id #uuid "b21741da-13f0-5f26-8c92-b40d6cb5d2f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120807/selection/6ed7541656a78e913aa4a29fcc63f14df4ad943c9afe513ee16462bc07eb26b0" :answer/id #uuid "cc04feb7-3169-5f7e-8b7c-361f57dc70f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120807/selection/35c0d04af9622de3840be4b9057e0e217b5b397382260d5721b234450e0a3153" :answer/id #uuid "9c274948-0224-5037-a192-3ba9ae98